<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-660] Writing Protobuf messages with extensions results in an error or data corruption.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-660</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently, in ProtoParquetWriter there&apos;s not any support for extended protobuf messages. An attempt to write a protobuf message with extension either:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Results in an uninformative error like this:
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;parquet.proto.ProtoWriteSupport: Cannot write message 
YOUR_EXTENSION_TYPE cannot be &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;cast&lt;/span&gt; to A_BASE_FIELD_TYPE : BASE_FIELD_NAME 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Results in a data corruption, if an extension type is compatible with a base field type with a corresponding index.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Imo there are two possible solutions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. Ignore extension fields.&lt;br/&gt;
2. When an extension field is detected in a message, throw an informative error.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
